A||||4||fyerstarter||Idles at 1500 + Check Engine light after driving for a while||||1||
Z||000000||fyerstarter||04-09-2001||04:54 PM||||I found this article at fieroowners.com  <P><B>Question: My question is about the idle on my Fiero. First, it's a '86 SE V-6 with 109K miles. Just recently I noticed that driving on the freeway the check engine light would light up. The car seems to be running fine though. If I shut off theengine and restart it, the light would not come on until some more freeway driving. In town the light is off. Another symptom is that now in the mornings I'll start the engine up to about 2000 rpms and stay there for a while cold. It has never idled up that high before, even cold! Then as it warms up, the idle will drop down to about 1600 and stay there. The only time it will drop down below 1600is if it sits and idles for an extended period of time and temp climbs up over the normal operating temp. The original idle speed seemed to be around 900 rpms. If you caould give me some place to look to fix these problems I'd appreciate it. I really don't want to take it to the dealer, because the basic repair quote from them seems to be $300 for everything they do to my Fiero. Regards TC <P>Answer: Welcome to the world of Fiero reality. The problem with your Fiero sounds like the EGR tube. The only place to get one is from the dealer. The price he quoted you isn't too out of line. The average price for the EGR tube is around $100. You have no choice. You have to replace the EGR tube, and your choices are for you to fix it or pay the dealer. </B><P>I have these exact same symptoms except for when the car first starts up it idles at about 900rpm for no more than 5 mins and then jumps up to 1500. I havent had a chance yet to check the codes yet but I have examined my EGR tube and there are no cracks in it. Forgive my ignorance but what exactly does the EGR tube do and is there a way that it can be hosed even if it appears intact? Anyone have any other ideas what could be causing this?<P>Any advice is appreciated. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||04-09-2001||06:39 PM||||The cracked EGR tube is for all basics a vacuum leak. Any vacuum leak can cause the problem. I had a high idle with the same symptoms described in the "letter" it turned out to be the vacuum line from the purge canister got too close to the "y" pipe and melted. Replaced vacuum line all better. 3 years ago I had numerous vacuum leaks. There are 5-6 vacuum lines that run under the top plenum and these are hard plastic. They can crack and split causing the same symptoms. My suggestion is to check all vacuum lines. The EGR itself can go bad too. Besides, It said in the letter $100 for the EGR tube from a dealer only!?! IRM sells a flexable one. I have 2 tubes at home from bone yard runs. I know I have seen other places sell the EGR tubes and if I remember the most expensive I've seen them was around $60.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fyerstarter||04-09-2001||11:02 PM||||Thanks Orief, Ill check for vaccuum leakage.||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||04-10-2001||03:58 PM||||Clear the codes first then go drive it until the lite comes on, then check the code. The code will narrow down the search for the problem. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||04-10-2001||07:18 PM||||i got my egr tube from chevy S10 pu. same as orig. It was such a pain to change Im going with the IRM stainless braided next time.||||reg||1
